Narrative Maps implementation and ROGER dataset
-----------------------------------------------

`library/narrative_maps.py`, `data/ROGER_images/` and
`data/roger_ground_truth.json` derive from:

    faustogerman/ROGER-Concept-Narratives
    https://github.com/faustogerman/ROGER-Concept-Narratives
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Fausto German

which accompanies:

    German, F.; Keith, B.; Matus, M.; Urrutia, D.; Meneses, C.
    "Semi-Supervised Image-Based Narrative Extraction: A Case Study with
    Historical Photographic Records." arXiv:2501.09884, 2025.
    (Reference [11] of the present paper.)

Specifically:

  * `library/narrative_maps.py` is adapted from upstream `narrative_maps.py`.
    The changes are listed in that file's module docstring: the sliding-window
    dictionaries were made module-level globals, `solve_LP` was added to build
    the CLIP-based similarity tables and drive the linear program, and two
    unused parameters were dropped.

  * `data/roger_ground_truth.json` is upstream `ground_truth.json`, byte for
    byte. It holds the six expert-curated baseline storylines and the 34
    seed labels used for semi-supervised label spreading.

  * `data/ROGER_images/` is the 501-image ROGER photograph set from upstream
    `roger-dataset/`, byte for byte. Upstream additionally ships a cached DETR
    embedding file inside that folder; it is not used here and is not included.

Earlier revisions of this repository also carried upstream's `helpers.py`,
`main.ipynb`, `extraction-pipeline.png`, `results-high-d.pkl` and
`results-low-d.pkl`. None of them are used by the experiments in this paper
(which use CLIP embeddings, not DETR), so they have been removed. They remain
available upstream and in this repository's git history.


Narrative Maps algorithm
------------------------

The algorithm itself is from:

    Keith Norambuena, B.F.; Mitra, T. "Narrative Maps: An Algorithmic Approach
    to Represent and Extract Information Narratives."
    Proc. ACM Hum.-Comput. Interact. 2021, 4, 228.


Photographic archive
--------------------

The photographs are from the Robert Gerstmann Fonds at Universidad Catolica
del Norte, which provided access to the archive. Please retain this
acknowledgement in any derived work.


Models
------

Evaluation used OpenAI GPT-4o via the OpenAI API, and Qwen2.5-VL-7B served
locally through Ollama. Visual features use OpenAI CLIP
(`openai/clip-vit-base-patch32`) via Hugging Face Transformers. Each is subject
to its own licence and terms of use.
